    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="d330-01" n="1" xml:id="d330-01"/>

                <head>330. Telegram 4515 From the Embassy in Afghanistan
                    to the Department of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d330-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d330-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName>Kabul</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1969-09-04T08:35:00+00:00">September 4, 1969, 0835Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subj:</label>
                    <item>Conte Amendment</item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>Ref:</head>
                    <item>State 146191</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>In call on Farhadi, Director
                        General Political Affairs in Fon Off, Aug 30 I told him I was under
                        instructions raise purchase SU-7s in light Conte Amendment. I reviewed
                        legislative history and gave him copy of relevant protions of Foreign
                        Assistance Act. I particularly drew his attention to language that “the
                        President is directed...” and explained to him that executive branch of
                            USG had no rpt no alternative but to
                        investigate thoroughly purchase of sophisticated equipment by country to
                        which US extending aid.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I then explained that to determine applicability of Conte Amendment we
                        needed information on date of firm arragenements for SU-7s and financial
                        details (para 5 reftel).</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>
                        Farhadi said he would be in touch
                        with us soon on my approach.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>Neumann</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d330-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d330-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files
                    1967–69, DEF 19–6 USSR–AFG. Secret. Repeated to
                        DIA.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d330-f2" n="2" xml:id="d330-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador Neumann reported that, as
                    instructed, he had met with Afghani Deputy Foreign Minister Farhadi and raised the issue of the purchase
                    of the SU–7s and the possible impact on U.S economic assistance to Afghanistan.
                        Neumann asked for details concerning
                    the purchase.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
